A||||8||87ECO5||Taking a moment to say THANK YOU!||||4||
Z||000000||87ECO5||03-22-2000||10:02 AM||||There's been a small cloud of negativity on the forum lately.  I hope to reverse some of it by taking a moment to show my appreciation to a few members:<P><B>william_thorniii and fiero56</B> - For being extremely generous, always willing to lend help, advice, parts and tools, and for being so thoughtful, courteous and tolerant of my family.<P><B>2M4 Dale</B> - For making me laugh every morning with a joke or two in my inbox and for being so trusting to invite a total stranger into your home simply because he owned a Fiero.<P><B>Monkeyman</B> - For making me laugh with his wonderful sense of humor and making me happy with his overwhelming sensitivity.<P><B>BENGAL4 and BOILERMAKER</B> - For being supportive of me and my ideas, for complimenting my efforts, and for providing valuable advice that's helped me.<P><B>ChadMan</B> - For being extremely generous, always willing to lend help and advice, and for taking the time to always keep me up to date on the latest and greatest in engine swaps!<P>I'd also like to thank everyone that ever assisted me with a problem, who listened while I vented about school shootings and the harming of animals, who complimented me on a job well done (my engine detailing and Fiero drawings, for instance), who showed interest in and provided support on my ideas (the cookouts, the road trips, the modified HVAC panels, etc.).<P>I singled out the people above because I talk with them on an almost daily basis and I feel we've established a very strong friendship - one that I'll treasure for a long, long time!  YOU GUYS ARE THE GREATEST!!!!!<P>Thanks, folks.  <B>I REALLY APPRECIATE YOU!</B>||||reg||4
