Z||000006||william_thorniii||03-23-2000||07:17 PM||||87EC05,<P>It sure doesn't take much to make you happy.  Seriously though anything that I can ever do to help, just let me know.  I am just excited to find other Fiero-holics here in the area to share experiences and tips with.  <P>On another yet related note... I have been just dying for you to let me buff your paint.  Your car is immaculate, except the finish.  If I buff it out then you can just apply a coat of wax to the top and she will look better than new.  It will only take me a few hours to do the high-speed buff job.  The biggest part of the job will be your part, waxing, window clening, tire dressing...  Perhaps this weekend sometime... e-mail my work account if you are interested (bthorn@sheffield-cmm.com).  If we can't use your driveway... we can break into the shop here at work :P  No body is here on the weekend except me.  While I am at it, I might just buff out the paint on my '85.  It could use it.  <P>Chadman,<P>I'm still out here, just not so often.  Thanks for noticing.  I am working like crazy still, but also the company is trying to crackdown on internet "clicks".  The sad part is that they do not look at time spent here at work, just clicks.  Therefore since I spend a lot of time here, I really have to cut back on my presence here.  I am sure that some will be very happy to see that.  <P>I am Lookin' forward to the upcoming cookouts/events though, but all these great Fiero activities are going to make it hard to get out to NJ to pick up my newest ride.  <P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||14
Z||000007||fiero56||03-23-2000||09:43 PM||||I have been very excited about meeting Fiero owners in my area. I had no idea there were so many enthusiasts near me. Plus, it makes boring weekends in the winter much more bearable, having Fiero folks to talk with. <P>William, I am sure by now that you noticed by now that my Fiero badly needs a good buffing. I'll let you know if you can touch my paint after I see how Scott's came out <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">. j/k, If I'm in a good mood, I might even be willing to pay you. Let me know if your interested. I'll send you an e-mail too. Fiero folks are the greatest aren't they?!||||reg||1
Z||000008||william_thorniii||03-24-2000||01:02 PM||||56,<P>No problem.  I am sure that we can work something out.  I do hate to be the bearer of bad news though... but Scott's car will turn out better.  The paint is in worse condition on the surface but does not appear to be missing anywhere.  Then of course you have the black car thing going against you.  This weekend looks promising.  Can we use your garage?  <P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||10
